# File: tests/blender/test_contract_validate.py, tests/blender/test_inspect_spatial.py
# Generated from: specs/153-report-sample-locations-in-geometry-contract-findings/requirements.md
Feature: Report sample locations in geometry contract findings

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Duplicate-vertex finding locates the duplicates
    Given a transformed mesh of two joined closed boxes that share one vertex position, each box in its own vertex group
    When contract validation runs on the asset
    Then the geometry.duplicates finding has a count of the duplicate vertices
    And each sample gives the world-space position, the vertex index, the coincident vertex index, and both boxes' vertex groups

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Face findings locate the faces
    Given a mesh with zero-area faces and a mesh with inward-flipped faces
    When contract validation runs
    Then geometry.zero_area and geometry.normals carry count and samples with face index, world-space face center, and vertex-group names

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Loose-vertex finding locates the vertices
    Given a mesh with loose vertices
    When contract validation runs
    Then geometry.loose carries count and samples with each loose vertex's index, world-space position, and vertex-group names

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Samples are capped and deterministic
    Given a mesh with more than 5 offending elements for a geometry rule
    When contract validation runs twice on the unchanged asset
    Then count is the full total, samples are exactly the first 5 by ascending index, and both runs match

  @SCN005
  Scenario: Elements outside any vertex group
    Given a mesh with a geometry defect and no vertex groups
    When contract validation runs
    Then each sample's vertex-group list is empty and the finding is otherwise complete

  @SCN006
  Scenario: Spatial inspector carries the same detail
    Given an asset part with a geometry defect
    When the spatial inspector reports that part
    Then its geometry entries carry the same count and samples as contract validation

  @SCN007
  Scenario: Clean meshes are unchanged
    Given a mesh with no geometry defects
    When contract validation and the spatial inspector run
    Then no geometry findings are emitted and pass/fail results are unchanged
